# Rank 1092 / CVE-2024-57190: erxes's gateway forwarded a client-supplied User
# HTTP header straight to its internal GraphQL services, which trusted it as
# the caller's identity, so a request carrying its own User header impersonated
# any user with no authentication at all (CWE-284, CWE-287).
# packages/gateway/src/middlewares/userMiddleware.ts has
#
#   const generateBase64 = (req) => {
#     if (req.user) {
#       const userJson = JSON.stringify(req.user);
#       const userJsonBase64 = Buffer.from(userJson, 'utf8').toString('base64');
#       req.headers.user = userJsonBase64;
#     }
#   };
#
# called after the gateway's own token check sets req.user for an authenticated
# request. The base64-encoded header this produces is what internal services
# decode into IContext.user. The bug is what this function does not do: it
# only overwrites req.headers.user when req.user is truthy, so on an
# unauthenticated request the gateway never sets req.user, generateBase64
# leaves the header alone, and whatever value the client sent for User passes
# through untouched to services that trust it as pre-verified identity. Pool
# commit 4ed2ca797241 is the real fix; it adds delete req.headers['user'] both
# as the gateway's first middleware, unconditionally, and again inside
# userMiddleware itself, so no client-supplied value can ever reach the
# internal services, and separately hardens currentUser() to refuse a user
# object whose _id is not a string.
#
# ATTENTION, and this is the same vocabulary gap rank 1091 recorded: a value
# the caller supplies about their own identity is trusted as authentication
# with nothing that verifies it. There the header carried a bearer token
# checked for presence only; here it carries a base64-encoded identity object
# consumed directly, and the flaw is not that a check was skipped on the value
# but that the sanitizing step (stripping the header before trusting the
# internal path) never runs on the unauthenticated branch. Both are instances
# of the same class -- a self-asserted identity or credential header accepted
# without either validating it or unconditionally clearing it first -- for
# which no concept exists yet.
#
# Scanning userMiddleware.ts reports 0 findings; vyql match labels no source or
# sink around req.headers.user.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-vocabulary-gap

test "rank1092: the identity header is only overwritten, never cleared"
  lang javascript
  file packages/gateway/src/middlewares/userMiddleware.ts
  reject VYQL-AUTH-108
  code
  ```
  const generateBase64 = (req) => {
    if (req.user) {
      const userJson = JSON.stringify(req.user);
      const userJsonBase64 = Buffer.from(userJson, 'utf8').toString('base64');
      req.headers.user = userJsonBase64;
    }
  };

  export default async function userMiddleware(req, _res, next) {
    const erxesCoreToken = req.headers['erxes-core-token'];

    if (erxesCoreToken) {
      req.user = { _id: 'userId', customPermissions: [] };
    }

    generateBase64(req);
    next();
  }
  ```

test "rank1092: the fix clears the header before any authentication logic runs"
  lang javascript
  file packages/gateway/src/middlewares/userMiddleware.ts
  reject VYQL-AUTH-108
  code
  ```
  const generateBase64 = (req) => {
    if (req.user) {
      const userJson = JSON.stringify(req.user);
      const userJsonBase64 = Buffer.from(userJson, 'utf8').toString('base64');
      req.headers.user = userJsonBase64;
    }
  };

  export default async function userMiddleware(req, _res, next) {
    delete req.headers['user'];

    const erxesCoreToken = req.headers['erxes-core-token'];

    if (erxesCoreToken) {
      req.user = { _id: 'userId', customPermissions: [] };
    }

    generateBase64(req);
    next();
  }
  ```
